wlanpi-webui (1.8.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a Flipper Zero-style tile launcher at / (dark "device screen", app
    tiles, status strip). LibreSpeed moves to /speedtest/librespeed.
  * Source the /network cards (reachability, public IP, eth0 IP config,
    LLDP/CDP neighbours) from the wlanpi-core API instead of running shell
    scripts as the unprivileged webui user. This fixes the Reachability card
    always reporting "Arping Gateway: FAIL" (#108).
  * make_api_request now issues the requested HTTP method, so GET endpoints
    (e.g. /api/v1/utils/reachability) can be called with the HMAC signature.
  * Replace the per-app navbar dropdowns with an Apps page (/apps) that
    consolidates control for Speed Test, Profiler, Kismet, Grafana and
    Cockpit, and add a Settings page (/settings) for About, the dark-mode
    toggle, Debug and logout.
  * Remove all iframes. Cockpit and the Kismet/Grafana UIs open in a new
    tab; Speed Test navigates in the same tab, with a link back home on its
    pages.

